SPRINT 1 — COMPLETE

Goal
----
Prove the minimum viable Dream lifecycle:

Player sleeps
→ Dream session is created
→ Player enters custom Dream dimension
→ Session timer expires
→ Player returns to original location

Completed
---------
- Forge/Kotlin mod loads successfully
- Custom dream:dream dimension exists
- Sleeping in a bed triggers Dream entry
- DreamSession stores:
    - player UUID association
    - origin dimension
    - origin position
    - session end tick
- Server tick handler monitors active Dream sessions
- Player automatically wakes after session expiration
- Player returns to stored Overworld bed position
- Basic /dream enter and /dream exit debug commands exist
- Tested successfully in integrated server

Current Prototype Behavior
--------------------------
- Dream duration is currently 10 seconds / 200 ticks
- Dream dimension is currently a flat test world
- Dream entry currently teleports player to fixed coordinates:
    x = 0.5
    y = 80
    z = 0.5
- Return position is stored as BlockPos
- Dream sessions are stored in memory only
- Session state is keyed by player UUID

Observed During Testing
-----------------------
- Bed event successfully triggers before normal sleep completes
- Cross-dimensional teleport works
- Server-tick-based timer works correctly
- Automatic return to the origin dimension works
- Dream sessions can be created and removed without crashing

