SPRINT 2 — DREAM LIFECYCLE HARDENING - Turn the Sprint 1 prototype into a reliable Dream lifecycle that
all entry and exit mechanisms use consistently.

NO DREAM ANCHOR ACTIVE
----------------------
Player uses bed
↓
Dream mod does nothing
↓
100% vanilla sleep behavior


DREAM ANCHOR ACTIVE
-------------------
Player uses bed
↓
Vanilla decides whether sleeping is allowed
↓
If vanilla rejects sleep:
    Dream does not start

If vanilla accepts sleep:
    Dream intercepts the successful sleep
    ↓
    DreamService.enterDream(...)
    ↓
    Player is no longer treated as a normal sleeper

Definition of Done
------------------

- One shared function/service handles Dream entry - COMPLETE
- One shared function/service handles waking - COMPLETE
- Bed sleeping and debug commands use the shared Dream lifecycle - COMPLETE
- A player cannot start a second Dream while already Dreaming - COMPLETE
- Beds cannot trigger another Dream while inside dream:dream - COMPLETE
- Beds cannot be usable inside a dream. - COMPLETE
- Dream entry uses a safe spawn position - COMPLETE
- Wake-up returns the player reliably to their stored origin - non issue, works as intended already. COMPLETE?
- Manual /dream exit and timed wake behave identically - COMPLETE

- Vanilla sleep behavior is preserved when Dream activation is inactive
- Dream entry only occurs when vanilla would normally allow the player to sleep
- Daytime sleep attempts do not trigger a Dream
- Sleep attempts blocked by vanilla conditions do not trigger a Dream
- Entering a Dream stops the player from being treated as a normal sleeping player
- Dreaming does not accidentally trigger or interfere with vanilla night skipping
- Normal players can still use vanilla sleeping mechanics without interference

- Existing Sprint 1 functionality still works
- No crashes during normal enter / wake flow
- No crashes during invalid or blocked sleep attempts

Observed during testing:
- Quitting while inside dream:dream destroys the in-memory DreamSession.
- On relog, the player remains in the Dream dimension but has no active
  timer and /dream exit cannot determine the return location.

Required:
- Dream session state must survive server shutdown / player relog.
